Why use a Universal Party Model?

This is a common enterprise pattern used in large insurance and financial systems because many entities share the same core attributes (name, address, contacts, documents, relationships). Rather than duplicating those fields across separate tables for customers, hospitals, brokers, repair shops, reinsurers, and employers, they all derive from a single parties entity with specialized extensions. It reduces redundancy, simplifies integrations, and supports future expansion.

This module underpins nearly every other domain in InsureIQ: Policies, Claims, Underwriting, Billing, CRM, Marketplace, AI Risk Scoring, Fraud Detection, and Analytics all reference these customer and party records.

